## Scope

This inventory identifies the application dependencies resolved for `eldoc-idp-web` from the supplied parent/core/web POMs. The fourth POM, `eldoc-base-api`, declares only provided dependencies. Test/build-only dependencies, unused dependency-management entries and elDoc's own artifacts are excluded from the third-party runtime inventory. A dependency is included if Maven resolves it at compile/runtime scope, even if another declaration uses a different scope.

The inventory is based on POM resolution, not inspection of your final custom Uber JAR/container. See README.md for the remaining release checks. Original combined upstream notices are preserved intact and can mention optional, test or build components; such mentions are not assertions that those components ship with elDoc.

## Payara Micro Community {{PAYARA_VERSION}}

The exact Maven Central `fish.payara.extras:payara-micro:{{PAYARA_VERSION}}` distribution's `MICRO-INF/legal/OPEN-SOURCE-LICENSE.txt` and `3RD-PARTY-LICENSE.txt` are included in [licenses/payara](licenses/payara/). They contain Payara's CDDL/GPLv2 licensing, the applicable Classpath Exception, and third-party terms. Follow those component-specific terms. Source: https://github.com/payara/Payara — release {{PAYARA_VERSION}}. No assertion is made here about whether your custom Payara distribution is modified.

## Native components supplied separately

The provided declarations specify Bytedeco OpenCV `4.11.0-1.5.12` and Tesseract `5.5.1-1.5.12`. Release-specific reference license texts for JavaCPP 1.5.12, JavaCPP Presets 1.5.12, OpenCV 4.11.0 and Tesseract 5.5.1 are supplied under `licenses/upstream/*-reference/`. They must be matched to your actual custom sources and build configuration. They do not establish coverage of Leptonica, OpenBLAS, image codecs, statically linked code or other native libraries.

ONNX Runtime and WebP ImageIO are separately present in the Maven runtime tree. Their collected notices are included. WebP's libwebp COPYING/PATENTS/AUTHORS were obtained from the exact submodule revision pinned by WebP ImageIO v0.1.6. Graal's shaded ICU 78.2 and XZ for Java 1.12 references were identified from the Graal release build manifest; their texts are included alongside the Graal module licenses. Model weights and runtime-downloaded assets require their own inventory if redistributed.

